<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basseterre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Basseterre is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and Nevis, on the south-west coast of the island of Saint Kitts. Founded by the French in 1627 after they and the English partitioned the island, it was the capital of the French part until the island was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> in 1713. It later became the seat of British colonial government and the capital of the independent federation in 1983.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basseterre.jpg" alt="Basseterre" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: giggel · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Kitts,_Karibik_-_Marina_in_Basseterre_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
